    awplus(config)# no aaa accounting login default
    awplus(config)# no aaa accounting update

    awplus# show running-config | include aaa|tacacs
    tacacs-server host 10.38.22.33 key 9 kh3afeSqzrMfJtQogCRezF0CmP35QlDTDuTr0FNzz7I=
    aaa authentication enable default local
    aaa authentication login default local
    (no `aaa accounting` line of any kind remains)

Under a 40 s capture, with a full VTY session (login, `show clock`, `enable`,
`configure terminal`, `end`, logout) **and** console commands driven through it:

    0 packets captured
    FILEWIN /var/log/tac_plus.acct ... new-bytes=0 new-lines=0 matched=0

**STEP 12 VERDICT: PASS.**  Every accounting mode this case configured removes completely:
zero records and zero packets under the same stimulus that produced 44 records and many
flows.  The server configuration left behind at this point is this case's own setup line, and
it was removed at teardown.

